      origins: 'Country/Region of Origin: Robstown, Texas, USA\nTime Period: Early 1900s (circa 1920s)\nCreator(s): Unknown (developed in Texas card rooms)\nEtymology: Named after Texas, where it originated, and "Hold\'em" refers to players holding their own cards while sharing community cards',
