        rules: {
          objective: 'Make the best five-card poker hand using any combination of your two hole cards and the five community cards. Win chips by having the best hand at showdown or by making all other players fold.',
          gameplay: 'Blinds. Deal 2 hole cards each. Pre-flop betting. Flop (3 community cards), turn (1), river (1). Betting after each. Showdown: best 5-card hand from 7. Win by best hand or all fold.',
          keyRules: [
            'Blinds: small blind and big blind (or dealer/non-dealer in heads-up). Big blind equals minimum bet.',
            'Each player receives two hole cards face down. No player may show hole cards before showdown.',
            'Four betting rounds: pre-flop (after hole cards), after flop (3 community cards), after turn (1 card), after river (1 card).',
            'Dealer burns one card before dealing each community round (flop, turn, river).',
            'Best five-card poker hand from the seven available (two hole plus five board) wins. Player may use 0, 1, or 2 hole cards.',
            'At showdown all active players must show both hole cards. Last bettor/raiser shows first; ties split the pot.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Starting Hand Selection by Position\n\n Position  Playable Hands \n-------------------------\n Early (UTG, UTG+1)  AA, KK, QQ, AKs, AQs \n Middle  Add: JJ, TT, AKo, AJs, KQs, QJs \n Late (Cutoff, Button)  Add: 99-22, ATs-A2s, KTs, suited connectors \n Blinds  Defend with wider range due to pot odds \nKey Principles\n1. Play tight in early position\n2. Loosen up in late position\n3. Raise more than you call\n4. Fold when beat\n5. Don't chase draws without odds",
          intermediate: "Continuation Betting\nBet flop after raising pre-flop (~60-75% of pot)\nMore effective on dry boards\nLess effective on coordinated/wet boards\nConsider opponent's range\nPot Odds and Equity\nCalculate: Call amount / (Pot + Call amount)\nCompare to chance of winning\nCall when equity > pot odds required\nPosition Play\nAct last = more information\nSteal blinds from late position\nControl pot size in position\nAvoid marginal spots out of position",
          advanced: 'Range Analysis\nThink in ranges, not specific hands\nConsider what hands opponent would play this way\nBalance your own ranges\nUse blockers to construct bluffs\nBoard Texture\nDry boards (rainbow, disconnected): Bluff more\nWet boards (two-tone, connected): Bet bigger for protection\nDynamic boards: Consider future streets\nStatic boards: Current hand strength matters more\nGame Theory Optimal (GTO) vs Exploitative\nGTO: Unexploitable baseline\nExploitative: Deviate to maximize profit vs mistakes\nAgainst unknowns: Play GTO\nAgainst known mistakes: Exploit',
